Has anyone else played Dungeon of Doom on the Macintosh?  Probably not.
Well anyway, it is very close to hack and probably was put out when there
were many Dungeons-and-Dragons type programs around.

Characters have the ability to "partially identify".  In its "rumors" it
includes the following lines :

  Wizards knows wands.
  Jewellers knows gems.
  Knights knows armor.
  Jewellers knows rings.
  Fighters knows weapons.
  Sage knows scrolls.

eg. If a Knight picks up chain mail armor, it says :

  chain mail      <- probably chain mail +0
  chain mail +2 ? <- probably chain mail +2 or some other modifier.
                     (possibily -ve).

The ? remains until the item has been identified by a scroll of similar
means.  The guess at the modifier (I suppose) improves with character
experience.

So my vote is for "partial identify" for character classes.

